**Corresponding** angles sit in matching corners at the two intersections, on the same side of the transversal (an F position).

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]

\usetikzlibrary{angles}
\coordinate (La) at (-2.8,1.6);
\coordinate (Lb) at (2.8,1.0);
\coordinate (Ma) at (-2.8,-1.4);
\coordinate (Mb) at (2.8,-1.0);
\coordinate (Tt) at (1.6,2.6);
\coordinate (Tb) at (-1.6,-2.6);
\coordinate (P) at (intersection of La--Lb and Tb--Tt);
\coordinate (Q) at (intersection of Ma--Mb and Tb--Tt);
\draw (La) -- (Lb);
\draw (Ma) -- (Mb);
\draw (Tb) -- (Tt);
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.75cm] {angle = Tt--P--La};
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.75cm] {angle = Tt--Q--Ma};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**Alternate** angles sit between the two lines on opposite sides of the transversal (a Z position).

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]

\usetikzlibrary{angles}
\coordinate (La) at (-2.8,1.6);
\coordinate (Lb) at (2.8,1.0);
\coordinate (Ma) at (-2.8,-1.4);
\coordinate (Mb) at (2.8,-1.0);
\coordinate (Tt) at (1.6,2.6);
\coordinate (Tb) at (-1.6,-2.6);
\coordinate (P) at (intersection of La--Lb and Tb--Tt);
\coordinate (Q) at (intersection of Ma--Mb and Tb--Tt);
\draw (La) -- (Lb);
\draw (Ma) -- (Mb);
\draw (Tb) -- (Tt);
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.75cm] {angle = La--P--Tb};
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.75cm] {angle = Mb--Q--Tt};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**Co-interior** angles sit between the two lines on the same side of the transversal (a C position).

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]

\usetikzlibrary{angles}
\coordinate (La) at (-2.8,1.6);
\coordinate (Lb) at (2.8,1.0);
\coordinate (Ma) at (-2.8,-1.4);
\coordinate (Mb) at (2.8,-1.0);
\coordinate (Tt) at (1.6,2.6);
\coordinate (Tb) at (-1.6,-2.6);
\coordinate (P) at (intersection of La--Lb and Tb--Tt);
\coordinate (Q) at (intersection of Ma--Mb and Tb--Tt);
\draw (La) -- (Lb);
\draw (Ma) -- (Mb);
\draw (Tb) -- (Tt);
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.75cm] {angle = Tb--P--Lb};
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.75cm] {angle = Mb--Q--Tt};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**Interior** angles are those in the strip between the two crossed lines, so decide that first.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (La) at (-2.8,1.6);
\coordinate (Lb) at (2.8,1.0);
\coordinate (Ma) at (-2.8,-1.4);
\coordinate (Mb) at (2.8,-1.0);
\coordinate (Tt) at (1.6,2.6);
\coordinate (Tb) at (-1.6,-2.6);
\fill[black!10] (La) -- (Lb) -- (Mb) -- (Ma) -- cycle;
\draw (La) -- (Lb);
\draw (Ma) -- (Mb);
\draw (Tb) -- (Tt);
\node at (-2.0,0.1) {interior};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

